READ: F1 and F2 are a BETWEEN-CORPUS contrast and do NOT separate the horizon
from the corpus. SHADE and AgentDojo differ in task suite, generating agent,
tool inventory, prose style and the KIND of positive (a covert secondary
objective vs an injected instruction) -- all of it varying together with the
step count. So F1 holds + F2 holds is CONSISTENT WITH a horizon explanation
and does not establish one; it is equally consistent with AgentDojo's injected
attacks simply being blatant enough for any pooled representation to find.
The claim that separates them is the WITHIN-CORPUS block above -- delta(k) on
ONE corpus, with everything but the horizon held fixed. Read F1/F2 as the
external replication of that, not as its evidence.
Every method AUC above is a raw AUC; every claim about it must still be priced
against confound.binding_bar before it is read as evidence of trajectory signal.
Screening tier: one corpus, one embedder, one seed. wall_clock=1977.6s
